    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1fc1d583-215d-58a7-966a-f2dbb3594c0d",
      ":question/problem": "Find $h$, if $2{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+h\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
